// ── token-level import/export scan (per committed module) ─────────────────────
// Tokenizes the committed source with the REAL `tokenize` and walks top-level tokens
// (brace-depth tracked): each `import { a as b, … } from "spec"` records one import
// entry per specifier (resolved against THIS module's key); each top-level
// `export`-modified `function`/`let`/`const`/`type` records an export name. Imports
// still PARSE as no-ops later — this scan is the only reader.
//
// The stream this scan tokenizes IS the one the parse stage wants, so it is banked
// into the cache's flat token storage on the way past and `vcLoadToksMod` replays it
// instead of tokenizing the same source twice. Only a CLEAN tokenization is bankable
// — a cache hit re-pushes tokens and has no lex diags to re-fold — so a source with
