// A BLOCK-LOCAL TYPE NEEDS NO SHADOW ENTRY, and since D1045 that is a statement about
// the mangling, not the language: the parser mints such a declaration under a unique
// name (`P` → `P$b7`) and spells every reference at it, so by merge time there is
// nothing for `modShadow` to hide. What the merge must not do is visit one TWICE —
// `modRwStmt`'s `Program` arm skips it, because this scanner sees only "an identifier
// run" and would rename the `P` of `P$b7` against a top-level `P`. Both halves of the
// walk are the leaf's (W8): `tyname.nameIdentChar` and `tyname.skipQuotedName`. The
// quote arm is unreachable on a program that parsed, and stays so the pass is total.
